WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:04.650
So, it's finally elections season.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.490
It'll be an historic first 
prime minister elections by

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.290
smart phone vote on the GALAX platform.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.990
Who will the Japanese people choose?

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:16.740
What the polls have shown today is this:

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:17.230
<b>The Smartphone Prime Minister Elections Have Begun: 
What Will the People Decide?</b>

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:22.940
<b>The Smartphone Prime Minister Elections Have Begun: 
What Will the People Decide?</b>

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:22.940
<b>Sugayama Seitarou (73%) 
 Kuroiwa Dansaku (13%) 
 Yoshikawa Yuuki (8%) 
 Other (6%)</b>

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.850
The incumbent, Prime Minister Sugayama, 
is crushing the competition.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.960
He holds more than 70 percent of the votes.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.260
Suga-yan's way too strong!

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.810
But these are just poll results.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.420
We still have a week 
until the actual elections.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.830
All the candidates still have a chance.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:37.550
The one I'm particularly intrigued by...

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.470
is this one! Gelsadra-kun.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.540
<b>Gelsadra 
 Projected Votes: 1.9%</b>

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.900
He's the first alien prime 
minister candidate in history.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.510
And he's going to be coming 
by our show later on!

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.120
Tell me...

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.700
your...

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.510
desires!

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.880
I see...

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.590
I get it now!

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.880
<i>Oh, I believe he's here!</i>

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:17.250
It's unusual for Leader 
and Utsutsu not to be around.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.550
<i>Allow me to introduce 
to you our semi-regulars,</i>

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:23.380
<i>who, despite having super busy schedules 
during election campaign season,</i>

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:22.090
Pai-pai said something about standing 
up for the future and left.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:23.440
What's that about?

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.660
<i>are still coming today—</i>

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.980
<b>TV Exclusive: The first alien candidate in history, Mr. Sadra! 
 Why did he decide to run in the prime minister elections?</b>

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.980
<i>Gelsadra-kun and Tsubasa-chan!</i>

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.480
<b>Alien 
Gelsadra</b>

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.480
<i>Hello!</i>

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:30.770
<b>Gatchaman 
 Misudachi Tsubasa</b>

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:30.770
<i>Hello!</i>

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.190
<i>Hello!</i>

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.070
Well, Sadra-kun,

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.780
how confident do you feel about 
the prime minister elections?

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:58.930
<b>TV Exclusive: The First Alien Candidate in History, Mr. Sadra! 
 Why Did He Decide to Run in the Prime Minister Elections?</b>

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:41.130
<i>There's something I'd like 
to tell the viewers today.</i>

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:44.920
<i>It's what I can promise you 
if I become the prime minister.</i>

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.740
<i>Oh, that's what they call 
the manifest, right?</i>

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.540
<i>What's yours?</i>

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.200
<i>Please tell the camera. Go on!</i>

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:55.050
<i>If I become the prime minister,</i>

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.930
<i>I'll abolish CROWDS.</i>

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:02.570
Are CROWDS in big trouble?

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.250
Children are our most important treasure!

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.940
If I become prime minister,

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:41.950
I will direct my efforts to improving 
childcare and parent support services.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.820
<b>Please Vote for Paiman, 
Gatchaman Leader!</b>

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.820
Please vote.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.750
It's the Gatchaman panda.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.830
Wow! It's really moving.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.860
Look how popular I am.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.050
I've already won the first 
alien prime minister's seat.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.380
I'm going to be so busy!

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:55.380
I'm gloomy...

00:03:55.380 --> 00:04:00.880
<b>Paiman</b>

00:03:55.380 --> 00:04:00.880
Oh, this is the perfect time to make 
use of the politician's secretary!

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.840
<b>Come help. Urgent. 
 This is an order.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.180
Rui-senpai, what'd you 
want to talk to us about?

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:12.840
More importantly, are you recovering okay?

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:14.340
Take it easy.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:17.120
I'm sorry for making you worry.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.860
But I can't just lie around in bed.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:27.210
Gelsadra-kun, why would you abolish CROWDS?

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.480
I'm just listening to what everyone wants.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:34.420
If I grant their wish, 
they'll all be happy, right?

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.160
Their wish is temporary.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.630
They're just afraid right now.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:43.390
If they rely on others, 
they'll never develop self-motivation.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:46.770
Is this "self-motivation" really necessary?

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:53.350
Sorry. What you're talking about is too 
difficult for me to understand a whole lot.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.690
Can't the world be more simple?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.590
Help those in need.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.480
Protect those who are suffering.

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:05.110
Isn't doing that sort of thing 
what we're about as Gatchaman?

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:09.370
Tsubasa-chan, the world won't 
update if we only do that.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.120
What people want isn't an updated world!

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:14.320
That's...

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.610
See, I told you.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.710
That's enough, Rui.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.880
I agree with abolishing CROWDS, as well.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:28.090
That's why I decided 
to help his election campaign.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.180
What?!

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.900
I figured you might need a mastermind.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.360
Yes, please!

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.600
Thank you.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.760
This is getting pretty complicated.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.560
What are you going to do, Hajime-chan?

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:45.070
I'm not sure.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.530
It's ready, Sugane-kun.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.810
Isn't this burnt?

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:52.800
I asked for it to be rare.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.450
<b>Forest Cafe Garden</b>

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.210
Hey, did you decide 
who you'll be voting for?

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.070
Sugayama-san, right?

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:59.470
Who else is there?

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:01.460
Right?

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:06.080
You know I'm supporting 
Prime Minister Sugayama, right?

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.530
If you're going to support Gelsadra-kun,

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:11.180
it means you'll be supporting the opposition.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:11.800
That's correct.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:15.970
You are my secretary,

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:18.520
but your thoughts are your own.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.120
Can I ask you something?

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:25.500
Is your goal still to achieve world peace?

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.510
Yes.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:31.400
Then I have nothing more to say.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:34.950
There's only one of me in this room.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.320
I have a plan.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:46.170
Let's begin.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.590
<b>PR Strategy for the Prime Minister Elections 
~How to get Sadra elected~</b>

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.140
Our biggest enemy is 
Prime Minister Sugayama.

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:52.490
But the widespread support 
he enjoys in the polls isn't real.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:55.790
His approval ratings continue to fall.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:07:01.950
So why would everyone vote for Sugayama-san 
even if his approval ratings are sliding?

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:03.980
They don't feel other choices are viable.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.820
Above all, that's the 
prevailing mood right now.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:08.420
The mood...

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.830
Changing their vote requires decision-making.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.770
But they're not seeing 
a compelling alternative.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:17.820
In the end, they're just 
going with the flow.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:22.460
They just have a vague sense that 
they can live with the status quo.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.100
Vague...

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:28.840
Yeah, that's how I might 
be making my choices, too.

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:32.300
That's the reality of this country.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:34.500
But that's why...

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.740
you have a chance to turn things around.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:41.910
Oh, it's Hajime-chan!

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:42.900
Really?!

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.340
H-Hello.

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.500
Can I shake your hand?

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:49.850
Sure.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:55.260
Hey, who are you going 
to vote for in the elections?

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.100
It's a secret.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:57.830
Huh?

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.700
Because it's an election.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.250
<b>Alien Candidate 
 Gelsadra</b>

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:05.250
Hello!

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:09.200
I'm Gelsadra. I decided to run 
for prime minister in the elections.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.470
I'm his cheerleader, Misudachi Tsubasa!

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:13.900
It's that alien.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.040
Sadra-chan.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:17.350
The girl next to him was amazing in Shibuya.

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:19.130
She's a Gatchaman, right?

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:22.610
I was little when I arrived on this planet,

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.790
but thanks to milk, I grew a ton!

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.480
Yeah, right!

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:35.910
Oh, excuse me.

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:38.350
I can carry that.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:40.370
Where do you live?

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.970
Oh, can you?

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.290
Aren't you working?

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.820
It's fine!

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:49.290
It's part of a hero's job 
to help people in need!

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:53.290
<i>Especially now that there are more 
efficient means of communication,</i>

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:58.880
<i>people look more favorably upon face-to-face 
communication, even if it's inefficient.</i>

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:03.310
<i>What will determine the election results</i>

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.510
<i>are neither CROWDS or political ideals.</i>

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:08.190
<i>It'll be the mood of the people.</i>

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:11.340
<i>We might be facing a head wind right now,</i>

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.110
<i>but even the smallest opportunity 
can turn things around.</i>

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:14.860
It's an act.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.920
It's fake. Creepy.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:20.050
But they're helping people. I respect that.

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:21.510
Sugayama's the best.

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.910
Can't there be someone else?

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:28.710
Please vote for Sugayama Seitarou.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.010
I thank you for your support.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.640
Good job, sir.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.550
Okay.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.220
I hear the polls place you 
at over 60% approval ratings.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.290
It'll be an easy win.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.560
It's been slowly sliding, though.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.060
I'm getting a lot of these, too.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.650
<b>I'll never vote for you. 
 Anti-CROWDS 
 I hope you lose.</b>

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:53.100
Who bothers saying "lose"? What's the point?

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.940
It's not productive, y'know?

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:58.100
I wonder if they're dumb.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.310
What?

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:03.040
The camera was still rolling...

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.000
Huh?

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:08.040
Did he say "dumb"?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.550
Who does he think he is?

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.500
<b>Who does he think he is?</b>

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:14.000
Rui, we have a situation.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.380
What's the matter, X?

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:18.660
<b>Who does he think he is?! 
 I'll never vote for you, bastard!</b>

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:19.550
<b>You looked like an idiot on camera!</b>

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.470
Crap!

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:35.900
<b>Shame!: Mr. Sugayama's Clueless in More Ways than One
 Instead of "luxurious," he said...?</b>

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:32.020
This is footage of Mr. Sugayama visiting

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:35.900
a new urban nursing home last month.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:37.730
Wow!

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:39.550
It's luxorous.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:42.280
I'd consider living here myself someday.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.080
Did you hear that?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.290
He said, "luxorous."

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.830
Luxorous!

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.730
There's no such word!

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:51.130
The correct term is luxurious.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:52.810
So embarrassing!

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:56.120
The leader of a nation, being unable 
to use even a word like that—

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:58.350
considering the snafu on-screen last month,

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:03.430
I don't blame people for thinking 
he doesn't deserve to be prime minister.

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:06.310
Oh, that's a bit harsh.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:10.730
<b>Switch Segment</b>

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:14.320
Switch to the live broadcast!

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:17.230
<b>Historic First! 
 The alien prime minister candidate, Gelsadra-kun</b>

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:20.130
Hello, we're broadcasting from Riverside 
Senshu in Nagaoka City, Niigata Prefecture.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.990
We have a wonderful guest with us today!

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:26.540
I want to unite everyone's hearts.

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:30.600
Once united, we'll have no need 
for a power that enables fighting!

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:36.020
Shhh. No.

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.300
Hush now.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:39.750
You don't have to hush her.

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:43.170
No one thinks she's being noisy.

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:45.850
It's good that she's so healthy.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.690
<i>Good. That's the way to go.</i>

00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:03.430
<i>That's... the way to go...</i>

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:05.910
How wonderful!

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:09.320
That wasn't easy to say, I'm sure.

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:14.290
It speaks to the kind of person Sadra-kun 
and his supporter, Tsubasa-chan, are.

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:19.130
So, their efforts as they continue 
their brave trek across Japan

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.700
appear to be swaying the people's hearts.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:23.680
Take a look.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:29.720
<b>Sugayama Seitarou (30%) 
 Gelsadra (20%) 
 Yoshikawa Yuki (11%) 
 Kuroiwa Dansaku (9%)</b>

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:27.220
Despite Prime Minister Sugayama's 
overwhelming lead earlier,

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.720
it's fallen to 30 percent.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:35.020
In contrast, Sadra-kun has steadily 
increased his margin to 20 percent.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:38.190
<b>Paiman</b>

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:38.190
Keep up the good fight, Sadra-kun!

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:41.650
If you promise to vote for me,

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:45.360
right now, I'll give you this stuffed animal!

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:49.200
Paiman-san?

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.450
Oh, Reika!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.470
Great timing.

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:55.060
Do you want a stuffed animal?

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.340
Are you aware of the 
Public Officers Election Act?

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.050
Hey, let go!

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:03.470
I'm the leader of the Gatchaman!

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:04.900
I'm gloomy...

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:05.510
Let go! Let go!

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.510
<b>Showing His True Colors?! 
 Prime Minister Sugayama Refuses to Eat Soup Kitchen Meal for Homeless</b>

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:11.770
That was because I'd just 
eaten lunch. I was full.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:11.770
<b>Loser 
 Be considerate! 
  So that's why you see homeless 
 You should've eaten 
 Don't make excuses</b>

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:12.710
What?!

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:16.270
<b>Scandal! 
 3 Days after the Tachikawa Incident 
 Eating Luxury Beef Stew!</b>

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:14.450
I can't?

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:16.270
I can't eat beef stew?!

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:21.480
<b>Seriously? lolll 
 High roller! 
Right after that tragedy... 
He's a goner 
 He was an idiot from the start
Profiting off our taxes
 I bet it's not sometimes!</b>

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:19.020
It's a once-in-a-while-thing.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.480
I don't eat it all the time.

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:24.950
Why do people have to obsess about this?!

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:25.280
<b>3000 yen for lunch? 
He's out of touch 
He thinks he's better than the rest of us  
My lunch was 300 yen (cry) 
 Scum</b>

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.120
Who cares about a 3000-yen beef stew?!

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.120
<b>Just look at him! 
 Now the truth comes out 
 Huh? What attitude 
 He's done for lol</b>

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.700
<b>Anti-Sugayama</b>

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:30.700
<b>NO!! To Re-electing Sugayama</b>

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:30.700
Suga-yan's done for!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:32.370
Did you know, Hajime-chan?

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:36.900
Primitives love to gang up on 
someone as soon as you give them

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:40.370
the "go ahead" sign to attack!

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.550
Really?

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:43.160
"Oh, he's a baddie!"

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:45.310
"On him, guys!'

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:46.970
"On him!"

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:50.180
They're just typing that shit 
in their rooms on their keyboards!

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:53.810
Is that how it is?

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:56.130
Oh, there's Hajime-chan again!

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:01.210
<i>Everyone, thank you so much 
for coming in this head!</i>

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:58.810
Look!

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:06.490
<b>Citizens Rush to Hear Mr. Sadra Speak!</b>

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.650
Gel-chan is so cute!

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.870
<i>I'm the alien, Gelsadra!</i>

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.790
Tsubasa-chan is cute, too.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:08.030
<i>I'm running for the prime 
minister's seat in this election!</i>

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:06.490
We're about the same age, aren't we?

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:09.730
You're yesterday's news, Hajime-chan.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:11.600
<i>The reason a recent arrival to this planet</i>

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:11.600
How do you feel right now?

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:13.190
Right now?

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:16.080
<i>would want to become prime 
minister is simple...</i>

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:16.080
Everyone's the same color.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.050
Oh, the election's tomorrow already.

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:22.340
You're right.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:24.390
Did you all decide who you're voting for?

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:27.180
Well, Gel-chan probably.

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.630
Yeah.

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:33.930
Tomorrow's the vote. 
Who are you gonna vote for?

00:14:33.930 --> 00:14:35.800
Not Sugayama.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:39.190
Yeah, who'd be suicidal like that?

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.720
My grandma said he was nice to her.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:43.230
You're such pushovers lol

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.280
I'm okay giving him a try.

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:48.270
Seriously? lol He's an alien lol

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:49.770
This nation's finished lol

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:51.320
He's better than Sugayama.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.740
I'm voting because Tsubasa-chan's cute.

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:56.170
Sadra's saying good stuff.

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:58.660
And he can win a real fight.

00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:04.170
Rui, shall I delete negative articles 
about former Prime Minister Sugayama?

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.240
No.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.210
Doing it will only have the opposite effect.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.220
But at this rate...

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:14.100
Jou-san...

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:18.910
Is your goal to become an ally 
to a privileged kind of justice?

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:30.080
It's finally the elections tomorrow.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.750
Thinking that made me nervous 
and turned my face bright red.

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.200
That's how it's always been!

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:45.320
Lastly, I'd like a comment from my 
staunchest supporter, Tsubasa-chan.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:52.220
Umm... Thanks for coming out 
in big numbers today.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:57.510
Gel-chan has promised to end CROWDS.

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:01.440
I don't think we need CROWDS anymore, either.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:04.020
Instead, I promise you

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:09.310
that in times of crisis, 
the Gatchaman— I will come help!

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:11.820
That's what heroes do!

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:16.200
Gel-chan and I will always protect you!

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:26.340
Why aren't you happy?

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:29.290
You don't become the same 
color as everyone else.

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:30.800
Always the weirdo.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.160
You're the weirdo, Jou-san.

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:35.250
You're thinking this isn't what you wanted,

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:37.780
but you still try to keep it going.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.390
It's not right.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:40.100
It's not.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:42.610
There was 188.

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:47.360
There were that many people injured 
during the Shibuya terrorist attack.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:50.990
That many people fell victim to CROWDS.

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:52.700
Above all...

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:55.990
one of us almost lost his life.

00:16:56.480 --> 00:17:00.520
Elections are intended to have 
each individual think for themselves

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:03.870
and choose the candidate they 
want to entrust the future to.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:09.580
This... having people choose with 
the flow... is definitely wrong.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.850
Yeah.

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:13.340
But still!

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:17.130
I can't let CROWDS roam free!

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.010
Even if the means are wrong,

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.720
this will achieve my justice!

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:23.850
I see.

